description: Keep documentation and ADRs in sync with code. Always applies.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Documentation

Update docs in the same change as the code when applicable:

- `README.md` (if it exists) for user-visible behavior or setup changes.
- `docs/framework/*.md` when the ADE itself changes.
- API docs and configuration docs (including `.env.example`) when interfaces or settings change.
- An ADR in `docs/framework/adr/` for every important architectural decision. Copy `docs/framework/adr/0000-template.md`, number sequentially (`ADR-XXXX`), fields: Context, Decision, Alternatives, Consequences, Status.
- Docs must describe what exists. Never document a feature that is not implemented; mark future work as "Planned".
